{
  "_comment": [
    "The Linux systems this app can install, and where the bytes come from.",
    "Generated from lollipopkit/shellbox-rootfs. This copy ships inside the",
    "app and is the floor: it is used on a first run, with no network, or",
    "when the fetched one fails verification. Being part of the binary it is",
    "as trustworthy as the app itself, so valid_until does not apply to it.",
    "",
    "A distribution carries several releases. The first is what a plain",
    "install gets; the rest are offered beside it. `branch` is what the",
    "package manager reads as its release, and it is also what decides",
    "whether one release is an update of another: 24.04.3 and 24.04.4 are",
    "both `noble` and one replaces the other, while 26.04 is not.",
    "",
    "Each release may carry a 'rootfs' block, the repacked artifact that",
    "repository publishes, and always carries 'upstream', the distribution's",
    "own file. Absent 'rootfs' means nothing has been repacked for it yet."
  ],
